      "content": "The \"Old Money\" consumer is characterized by a quiet, inherited elegance, favoring timeless, understated luxury that whispers rather than shouts. Their aesthetic leans toward classic tailoring, muted palettes, and heritage brands, projecting an air of effortless, established refinement. Conversely, the \"Mass-Market/Urban/Trendy\" consumer is defined by bold, fast-moving trends and visible status signaling. Their energy is loud and immediate, embracing streetwear, vibrant colors, and the latest viral fashion moments.",
